{"title":"2017 AIME I Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:50%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I\" title=\"2017 AIME I\">2017 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b>)<br /> <span class=\"noprint plainlinks\"> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2017\">AoPS Contest Collections</a> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/contest/download/c3416/2017\">PDF</a>\n</span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"font-size:80%;\">\n<p><font style=\"text-align:center;\">Instructions</font>\n</p>\n<ol><li>This is a 15-question, 3-hour examination. All answers are integers ranging from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc7ddbca9440579298bf24e0f9bcf2c0457bfc1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$000$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/0705411d92671faf1fe5602cfef8f353c7f0f83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, inclusive. Your score will be the number of correct answers; i.e., there is neither partial credit nor a penalty for wrong answers.</li>\n<li>No aids other than scratch paper, rulers and compasses are permitted. In particular, <u><b>graph paper, protractors, calculators and computers are not permitted.</b></u></li></ol>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Fifteen distinct points are designated on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />: the 3 vertices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> other points on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> other points on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />; and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> other points on side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb0f1d8a43539dbc3355734bafb2bfd855b5f87.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{CA}$\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />. Find the number of triangles with positive area whose vertices are among these <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> points.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>When each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/2/ae2f549965059c7e2b65c4366cfe542fc8fb8789.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$702$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/2/9c266575cf61d24ddc13eea9269f0d2e669c744a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$787$\" width=\"27\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/d/b7d05977e249669c8458358830f45ae647f965f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$855$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> is divided by the positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, the remainder is always the positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. When each of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/b/e9b5d09eb13ea060ab8b0ea4e789f4febf074397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$412$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/5/3c5d02d9b611a58da9a66f3dfd0220cba07dc611.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$722$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/9/ab93876fdf6ee6b0196ba14d6887fc8e5b189f7a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$815$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by the positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, the remainder is always the positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/8/268ab58b81e4c94d8fff6051a878e3aab9cb8a6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s \\neq r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"17\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/7/ae71390ee5850cfa5f2952a974fbf385bf83e41b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+r+s$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"113\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/1/8e137a585dc18a5612b4ef6e8297abdca3c6eb2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> be the units digit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/4/314149be9582842c3e8efe75b62a4f32fc1d3463.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 + 2 + \\dots + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"116\" height=\"13\" />. Find the remainder when\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c25a797fd18625aea3a70ae1b6906027405232ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{n=1}^{2017} d_n\\]\" width=\"46\" height=\"50\" />is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A pyramid has a triangular base with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/9/e290f2cba0ba0e11c0b91630da15a408da2fcf1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The three edges of the pyramid from the three corners of the base to the fourth vertex of the pyramid all have length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/6/66644fd9f411299c3c1eabf151b5f601c9ef6c21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$25$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The volume of the pyramid is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f1dcbb9badfd3447d4e7351678b7d71ea9bff6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m\\sqrt{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A rational number written in base eight is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/4/d84d6e699ad7bd05ea263e0df7e784ea174bac58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{a} \\underline{b} . \\underline{c} \\underline{d}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"40\" height=\"15\" />, where all digits are nonzero. The same number in base twelve is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/3/de3ed8ed28480d2829dc802c4a695697e6a5f345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{b} \\underline{b} . \\underline{b} \\underline{a}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"38\" height=\"15\" />. Find the base-ten number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/0/9a05e92524bfc79f60f4e4679588a8928a6db0b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underline{a} \\underline{b} \\underline{c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A circle circumscribes an isosceles triangle whose two congruent angles have degree measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />. Two points are chosen independently and uniformly at random on the circle, and a chord is drawn between them. The probability that the chord intersects the triangle is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9ed0bde97de96404449420f812178f5138f81521.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{14}{25}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />. Find the difference between the largest and smallest possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For nonnegative integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> with  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9ca1916e0fb190e4065dc6d1f50443be898f60db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b \\leq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/2/4925f1c0d17017eca80e96ae18746a8986bcb95a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(a, b) = \\binom{6}{a} \\binom{6}{b} \\binom{6}{a + b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"215\" height=\"53\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> denote the sum of all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/f/a/cfa78281fa5ccabc62b328a385ad5592fb5fd736.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$T(a, b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"18\" />, where  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are nonnegative integers with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9ca1916e0fb190e4065dc6d1f50443be898f60db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b \\leq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are chosen independently and uniformly at random from the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/9/0a95eb5723de89eb471db442c07341bacb4087e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(0, 75)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be two points on the plane with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54fba0a8adfc0dd5bd6ced7466206afe9af402fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP = 200$\" width=\"79\" height=\"12\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be on the same side of line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/d/25dcc9ecb8e7c6fb80766c186721353e6c3dc398.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that the degree measures of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/b/17b9d2af2ca2df699f4c00adc8215c1811f7e964.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle POQ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/6/5d6c9b25f1b709e60f5dc891b8aa147de21f9bf0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle POR$\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/5/9856a773bccb60f8b1cad7934a8d69c718042fba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle OQP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/3/fb3f4ade70624a2f4e495ffad581df0b90caf775.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ORP$\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> are both right angles. The probability that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/6/2d6148bd71ace95aeae89790f0cc2cc921999752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$QR \\leq 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"79\" height=\"16\" /> is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f583697295fc6f723862c13228ee55107c33ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"22\" height=\"34\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/b/53bf1afcb274a3bb84338109fffec8a1f1c02008.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/5/e25ba77d07ce9afa658be470625f0ebc30ff04b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{10} = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"65\" height=\"15\" />, and for each positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/6/9b6aa0da7eb9e90475050ffe98d9d9e8578c6c4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt;10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/f/fff571692d273c7e41e2650e18b9ecf9d47d10b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n = 100a_{n - 1} + n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. Find the least positive <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95a0855f86ecd8d81433e92418a0d484a3143d5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" /> is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/1/a313bf06349648df7be807bee95b651604ce7a7e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/f/06f8f4d0900a5a1d6b758942d89495a1085beb6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1 = 18 + 83i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"104\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b71a92ed21a4190add152815b756343bd0db366f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_2 = 18 + 39i,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/3/08301e00494fe7a2120412a191e2fc0e71128eb6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_3 = 78 + 99i,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"109\" height=\"16\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/c/dac5dec897250384833e3c1b44639bf91cca823a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = \\sqrt{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the unique complex number with the properties that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/0/fc08a4fe88cc4ddbb32fe9d66a3995f959f1befc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{z_3 - z_1}{z_2 - z_1} \\cdot \\frac{z - z_2}{z - z_3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"120\" height=\"35\" /> is a real number and the imaginary part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is the greatest possible. Find the real part of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider arrangements of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efeb79a949aeb0693f418254f577d452fa92b24.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, \\dots, 9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"92\" height=\"16\" /> in a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/7/d278803d72fcc493afb1559174a483aa7f41d143.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> array. For each such arrangement, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/9/5e97a8af68fbc8e357d3ee0eba452022b06c1875.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/572b65ebc3f438b176b4ca4a890799f2f72564af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> be the medians of the numbers in rows <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> respectively, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the median of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/1/631a440d1aed40fba8aa7838f617eb91cab3ecad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{a_1, a_2, a_3\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"84\" height=\"18\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> be the number of arrangements for which <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/a/11af515956d2fa847b77d1ae0e81258a08a55aa4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 5$\" width=\"48\" height=\"12\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/6/9866e3a998d628ba0941eb4fea0666ac391d149a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Call a set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> product-free if there do not exist <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/4/88479cba5eb99ebe10b309338f629abbdb657cb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a, b, c \\in S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"75\" height=\"16\" /> (not necessarily distinct) such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39c90dfd030d621c521b46fcd475f8593797c9aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a b = c$\" width=\"49\" height=\"12\" />. For example, the empty set and the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a77d2a88ffaaca488cb648f6ad218420d939adac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{16, 20\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"64\" height=\"20\" /> are product-free, whereas the sets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/5/075b5a77193485deeff645f6af2422cde2f0420b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{4, 16\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/e/11edd316199fc135c095b0a1bf3cf49716b6e055.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{2, 8, 16\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> are not product-free. Find the number of product-free subsets of the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/9/e0979c14592c31e07cc433960572b3e07d940c22.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1, 2, 3, 4, \\ldots, 7, 8, 9, 10\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"187\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6fa6546da3adb7c8422b7d96a499c43757390c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\geq 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/b/92b5d412e881e305eeacf03bc1d7b92276eda828.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Q(m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> be the least positive integer with the following property: For every <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/9/7f970221d3f8b67b181859de4bfed643760f3874.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq Q(m)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"78\" height=\"18\" />, there is always a perfect cube <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/b/7bb87766bcaaf492fc1be5874b732197f6f0d641.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"17\" /> in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d7757275e51022d6016af45ef9ecde4baa8440b3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &lt; k^3 \\leq mn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" />. Find the remainder when\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f783b9b05cb0664a228ffb322175c286e164a474.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sum_{m = 2}^{2017} Q(m)\\]\" width=\"74\" height=\"50\" />is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/735b4fd08c7f1e4d6d79c161a483417073efb9b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/6/3767f0665ea4d5f0e9c58452fc5782b42a8a65a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" /> satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/003301fe7b911c3e98b9edb848283faa3917419e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_a(\\log_a(\\log_a 2) + \\log_a 24 - 128) = 128$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"310\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/f/fcf9b03c88382c4e847395c392e6cbdfc57a05a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_a(\\log_a x) = 256$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"141\" height=\"18\" />. Find the remainder when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/e/6ee927e1332358c96c62c277441c907c4f51057f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The area of the smallest equilateral triangle with one vertex on each of the sides of the right triangle with side lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d590f3358bac936c098c5c9b60ecdf068b17371.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"33\" height=\"18\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/b/a7bbdd5c7b1b7126b91245e94896ebef4a4d6857.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt{37}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />, as shown, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/5/c2550b25192fc3384833c9da6ba36eabc93af418.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{m\\sqrt{p}}{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"32\" height=\"24\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a61870035304b46bdbcafc39d04bea20e3899c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"80\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/2040951aabf67ea7477c8aa658e56ccda3a56492.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(5cm); pair C=(0,0),B=(0,2*sqrt(3)),A=(5,0); real t = .385, s = 3.5*t-1; pair R = A*t+B*(1-t), P=B*s; pair Q = dir(-60) * (R-P) + P; fill(P--Q--R--cycle,gray); draw(A--B--C--A^^P--Q--R--P); dot(A--B--C--P--Q--R); [/asy]\" width=\"238\" height=\"168\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\"> Solution</a>\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I\" title=\"2017 AIME I\">2017 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2017\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2016 AIME II Problems\">2016 AIME II Problems</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_II_Problems\" title=\"2017 AIME II Problems\">2017 AIME II Problems</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2017 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php